  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The bats went silent when it mattered most.",
    "what_this_means": "They had the pitching. Lopez carved through 1.2 innings untouched, and Alvarado locked down two scoreless frames with three strikeouts. That was enough to win on any other night. But they scored once. Once. Against Chicago's rotation. Four runners left in scoring position. Empty at-bats in the sixth and ninth when the game was still there to take. The bullpen's clean work became meaningless when the offense couldn't deliver a single runner home after the first inning. This is not a slump showing itself quietly. This is the inconsistency that's defined the season showing up when the margin was thinnest.",
